{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506683-must-be-this-tall-to-be-a-world-power-reconciling-organizational-power-stats","id":1506683,"title":"Must Be This Tall To Be a World Power-Reconciling Organizational Power Stats","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-27T17:59:24-07:00","id":1506683,"title":"Must Be This Tall To Be a World Power-Reconciling Organizational Power Stats","content":"Immediately clarifying, I don't mean the actual Power (Reach, in the case of Curse) attribute, I mean Power Stat in the way that it would be applied to templates, specifically talking about Esotery, Dominance, and Standing.<br /> <br /> Okay, so this could actually be a bit of a conversation because of farther reaching implications, which is why this isn't in Ask a Simple Question.<br /> <br /> So ever since Geist: the Sin-Eaters Second Edition, we've had a steady roll out of organizational rulesets, the sort that's intended to tackle larger group where everyone is unlikely to know about everyone else, with it's culmination coming in Deviant: the Renegades (for which this ruleset was first imagined for), and with the Devoted Companion out to backers, it's proven to be a very power and useful toolset for what it's exactly meant to do-and more asides. As many people have pointed out, the Conspiracy rules are solid for creating any sort of organized society, in different levels of granularities. As a handful of examples, you could use it to model occult matrices in Descent, a freehold in harmony with each Court as their own branch wtih their own Hierarchical Node or a freehold more at a distance or odds with each other by giving each court their own full mockup, the various levels of Mage's sectarian organizations from the global perspective down into individual Caucuses/Assemblies and the Consiliums between that form from them, and even for mapping the global spread and quarantine of the Contagion (ala a near-Pandemic like implementation). It's versatile, is what I'm saying.<br /> <br /> But of course, each of these models aren't simply copy pasted-The system for Krewes has notable differences from the Cult system in Curse, and both are subtly different from Conspiracies in Renegades. On the whole, this is good, because these games are saying and doing something different with the rulesets in accordance to their own themes and mechanical structuring. But when we start cross-applying the tools, a thing does come up that becomes worth questioning, and that's the matter of scale.<br /> <br /> To best illustrate this, I'm going to hone in on Esotery against Standing*. See, Standing's pretty good for systems that are large for their tier, and it particularly stands out well for laying out globally wide organizations-you could very easily display the collective power, authority, and resources of the Mage Sects or the Arisen Guilds, as sideways examples. But despite being in a format that assumes a ready one to one, that's not the same assumption you could make with Esotery in Sin-Eaters. Esotery already represents something contextually different-there's a lot more emphasis on religious practice and spiritual belief as both &quot;glue&quot; and power as much as it represents institutional reach, presence, and influence-but going back to a bone dry comparison, a Krewe of Esotery 10 is just not the same as a Conspiracy of Standing 10-comparatively, you could make an argument, depending on the exact nature of the Krewe, it would have a Standing likely somewhere in the range of 5 to 8.<br /> <br /> Since there's a lot of utilization in implementing the Conspiracy Rules for these other communities, I figured it's probably worth having a chat on how to handle the disparity, or if that disparity is actually as much their as I assert it is (arguably, Esotery and Dominance can still be on scale with Standing, just more readily split between worlds). So, let's have that discussion.<br /> <br /> *Dominance from Curse, and Arisen Cults in general, are both pretty different that it becomes hard to cut lines across, and Cults sit in this weird range where it can both make a lot of sense to draw one-to-one with Conspiracies and not make a lot of sense to make those same drawings. The Arisen are complicated, who knew.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T11:11:15-07:00","id":1506768,"title":"","content":"I am planning on reading the Conspiracy rules soon. My Mage+Demon Chronicles tend to take place inside Seattle, which is also the sample city for Demon in general. So I'm thinking of using the Conspiracy rules to model a new Agency on the Demon side, as well as an organization akin to the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1476711-homebrew-rubber-band-society?p=1498276#post1498276\"><b>Ars Futuri</b></a> on the Mage side, with both of them working together to oppose the God-Machine and the Seers Of The Throne in Seattle, especially as it pertains to the Splinter Timelines. I might consult the Splintered City: Seattle supplement for guidance as well. The Agency and the Ars Futuri would join efforts to take control the Splinter Timelines connected to Seattle, so that the Seers of the Throne and the God-Machine cannot make use of these Splinter Timelines.<br /> <br /> In other words, they intend to build a futuristic utopia by reverse-engineering specific aspects of Splinter Timelines via a combination of magic and science. For example: that Splinter Timeline from the year 1999 that caused the Millennium Bug and destroyed the Internet has the Demon who uses the Cover of Carson Thurber, and is also the Fallen version of the Angel known as Y2K, who in turn is still loyal to the God-Machine in the dominant timeline. Carson Thurber could perhaps Hi-Jack the Angelic Cover of Y2K in a way that fully deactivates the Millenium Bug instead of postponing it indefinitely. I'll post the results in this thread once they are presentable, or maybe I should post them in the Mage or Demon forums?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 03-28-2023, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T17:38:52-07:00","id":1506808,"title":"","content":"This is a very odd thought that bubbled into my head on the drive home from work today: I suddenly began imagining how to use the conspiracy rules (specifically the parts about mapping nodes and their connections) as a novel way of representing Hedge navigation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T20:04:04-07:00","id":1506817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506683-must-be-this-tall-to-be-a-world-power-reconciling-organizational-power-stats?p=1506808#post1506808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a very odd thought that bubbled into my head on the drive home from work today: I suddenly began imagining how to use the conspiracy rules (specifically the parts about mapping nodes and their connections) as a novel way of representing Hedge navigation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting suggestion. Do you think the Thorn-Towns &amp; Hedge Settlements from Chapter 3 of Dancers In The Dusk could count as Conspiracy-Nodes? What about Hollows, Goblin Markets and Bastions?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T20:12:05-07:00","id":1506820,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how the current conversation is actually addressing the question, not gonna lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T20:18:34-07:00","id":1506821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506683-must-be-this-tall-to-be-a-world-power-reconciling-organizational-power-stats?p=1506820#post1506820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how the current conversation is actually addressing the question, not gonna lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry about that. I'll refrain from posting again in this thread until I have read the system in question more closely and have better commentary to give.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T21:10:57-07:00","id":1506825,"title":"","content":"So as far as the existing systems go, the Devoted Companion's expansion of the conspiracy mechanics actually has me thinking on Standing versus Dominance; stating outright that Resistance is never rolled for conspiracy actions makes it a little easier to align Reach and Grasp with Power and Finesse in comparable mechanics, for instance.<br /> <br /> I've remarked before on how conspiracies adding a lower fixed value to an Attribute for their Association makes them more fragile than an equivalent krewe or cult, but it's interesting to note that Fidelity being calculated off of the lower of a cult's two Attributes, combined with the cheaper dots from the Cult Merit capping at 5, incentivizes against skewing its legal and illegal influence too far in either direction.<br /> <br /> It's also interesting to note, bringing it back to krewes, that Congregation is the only Organizational Health Stat that actually models a state that can be directly harmed by killing its membership \u2014 Fidelity and Association represent faith and loyalty to the organization, whereas Congregation represents the membership's overall well-being alongside its unity and cohesiveness (Association also corresponds to the size of a conspiracy's following and can be damaged by massive loss of human life, but conspiracies occupy a narrative niche where goon combat is a feasible arrow in their quiver and krewes give an approximation for your group's NPC headcount by Resistance).<br /> <br /> Taking cues from these (and, to a lesser extent, Social Maneuvering's grounding in the assumption that the other party's continued trust in you is a legitimate stake), expanding the organizational rules to other gamelines might have to account for different functions \u2014 allowing Vampire to play the Institutional Corruption game means something different than modeling spirit-ecological give-and-take through the Web of Pain's mapping structure, and the way the God-Machine treats its tools means a set of Infrastructure treats crises of faith as either trivially unimportant or catastrophic depending on what's having them.<br /> <br /> On the topic of mapping Esotery to Standing, there's also the general scaling issue of the vast majority of krewes starting out with a foot in the door re: the Underworld where a conspiracy would need to be particularly high-powered or have an Icon lowering the effective scale of a Narrative Project to make headway in another world \u2014 the fact that most people who don't have major-template-level association with a given otherworld have to fumble around with Keys makes comparing a handful of death-divers and their ghost-and-medium support crew to a global conglomerate looking to frack The Oldest Oil gets a bit squidgy.<br /> <br /> Some of this is admittedly just rehashing the points addressed in the starting post, but it probably bears acknowledgement that the games have generally done fine with e.g. Shadow Potency and Rank not being wholly equivalent stats despite both functioning as Supernatural Tolerance ratings. I vaguely remember there being a Charm in Exalted that allowed you to act as an organization of a scale determined by your Essence, which might be an interesting concept for a power in any given other game or at least a basis for bridging the gap between &quot;here are two to five PCs&quot; and &quot;here is a Standing 1 organization.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T01:32:45-07:00","id":1506831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1506683-must-be-this-tall-to-be-a-world-power-reconciling-organizational-power-stats?p=1506825#post1506825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So as far as the existing systems go, the Devoted Companion's expansion of the conspiracy mechanics actually has me thinking on Standing versus Dominance; stating outright that Resistance is never rolled for conspiracy actions makes it a little easier to align Reach and Grasp with Power and Finesse in comparable mechanics, for instance.<br /> <br /> I've remarked before on how conspiracies adding a lower fixed value to an Attribute for their Association makes them more fragile than an equivalent krewe or cult, but it's interesting to note that Fidelity being calculated off of the lower of a cult's two Attributes, combined with the cheaper dots from the Cult Merit capping at 5, incentivizes against skewing its legal and illegal influence too far in either direction.<br /> <br /> It's also interesting to note, bringing it back to krewes, that Congregation is the only Organizational Health Stat that actually models a state that can be directly harmed by killing its membership \u2014 Fidelity and Association represent faith and loyalty to the organization, whereas Congregation represents the membership's overall well-being alongside its unity and cohesiveness (Association also corresponds to the size of a conspiracy's following and can be damaged by massive loss of human life, but conspiracies occupy a narrative niche where goon combat is a feasible arrow in their quiver and krewes give an approximation for your group's NPC headcount by Resistance).<br /> <br /> Taking cues from these (and, to a lesser extent, Social Maneuvering's grounding in the assumption that the other party's continued trust in you is a legitimate stake), expanding the organizational rules to other gamelines might have to account for different functions \u2014 allowing Vampire to play the Institutional Corruption game means something different than modeling spirit-ecological give-and-take through the Web of Pain's mapping structure, and the way the God-Machine treats its tools means a set of Infrastructure treats crises of faith as either trivially unimportant or catastrophic depending on what's having them.<br /> <br /> On the topic of mapping Esotery to Standing, there's also the general scaling issue of the vast majority of krewes starting out with a foot in the door re: the Underworld where a conspiracy would need to be particularly high-powered or have an Icon lowering the effective scale of a Narrative Project to make headway in another world \u2014 the fact that most people who don't have major-template-level association with a given otherworld have to fumble around with Keys makes comparing a handful of death-divers and their ghost-and-medium support crew to a global conglomerate looking to frack The Oldest Oil gets a bit squidgy.<br /> <br /> Some of this is admittedly just rehashing the points addressed in the starting post, but it probably bears acknowledgement that the games have generally done fine with e.g. Shadow Potency and Rank not being wholly equivalent stats despite both functioning as Supernatural Tolerance ratings. I vaguely remember there being a Charm in Exalted that allowed you to act as an organization of a scale determined by your Essence, which might be an interesting concept for a power in any given other game or at least a basis for bridging the gap between &quot;here are two to five PCs&quot; and &quot;here is a Standing 1 organization.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>It definitely clarifies and sharpens the original point, which will probably help point at good guidelines for adaptational purposes.<br /> <br /> The note about Esotery and Dominance both having the benefit of accomodating non-human, non-earthly actor resources was an acknowledgement about how supernaturally pillared organizations tend to have more equivalent &quot;Standing&quot; in their other worlds, Twilights, and slice of the night that humans don't occupy as much. A krewe may not be a global influence, but hell if a bad enough dude of one doesn't have the attention of a good amount of the upper reaches and plenty of the Deep Dominions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}